<%# locals: (example:, teams:, compact: false, board_style: false, hovered: false)

    A STATIC twin of contests/_multi_week_team_card, for the rules page.

    Why a twin and not the partial itself: the board card is a <button> wired to
    Alpine's toggleSelection and keyed on a live SlateMatchup id. The rules page
    has no contest, no cart and nothing to toggle — rendering the real one would
    mean manufacturing matchup rows to draw a picture.

    What is NOT duplicated is the part that would actually drift: every colour
    here comes from TeamColorsHelper#team_card_palette, the same helper the board
    uses, so re-tuning a team's brand re-colours this page in the same commit.
    `team` may be nil (a slug the DB has never heard of) — the helper is nil-safe
    and returns the neutral field, so the card still draws.

    board_style: true draws two details the way the real board card
    (contests/_multi_week_team_card) does, for /turf-monster-v2's phone mock:
      - the multiplier reads "1.1x Points", digits in mono and a lowercase x
        in the sans face, where the rules page says "1.1x Turf Score"
      - the opponent chips print emoji + the 2-3 letter abbreviation at one
        fixed size, never truncated (the default chips step up to text-sm at
        lg and truncate, which cut "IND" to "I..." inside the scaled phone)
    The number keeps ONE decimal on both styles (see the note below), so the
    phone agrees with the "1.0x" in the v2 page's own prose. Off by default:
    v1 renders unchanged.

    board_style also wraps the card in the board's own hologram shell
    (holo-wrap / holo-border / holo-card, application.css), and `hovered: true`
    gives it the board's lit state: the rotating ring in the team's alt colour
    and the 1.04 lift. A static page cannot hold :hover, so it wears
    .is-selected, which the board's stylesheet styles identically (minus the
    one-shot sheen sweep). %>
<% team = teams[example.team_slug] %>
<% pal  = team_card_palette(team) %>
<% if board_style %>
<div class="holo-wrap relative" style="--glow-c: <%= normalize_hex(team&.color_alt) || normalize_hex(team&.color_light) || pal[:accent] %>;"<%= ' data-test="phone-card-hover"'.html_safe if hovered %>>
  <span class="holo-border-glow" aria-hidden="true"></span>
  <span class="holo-border" aria-hidden="true"></span>
<% end %>
<div class="<%= 'holo-card relative ' if board_style %><%= 'is-selected ' if board_style && hovered %>rounded-2xl border-2 shadow overflow-hidden <%= compact ? 'p-3' : 'p-5' %> text-center"
     style="background: <%= pal[:gradient] %>; border-color: <%= pal[:border] %>; color: <%= pal[:fg] %>;<%= " --glow-soft: #{rgba(pal[:glow], 0.3)};" if board_style %>">
  <% if team&.location.present? %>
    <p class="<%= compact ? 'text-[10px]' : 'text-sm' %> font-medium leading-tight truncate"
       style="color: <%= pal[:location] %>"><%= team.location %></p>
  <% end %>
  <p class="font-extrabold leading-tight truncate <%= compact ? 'text-lg' : 'text-3xl' %>"
     style="color: <%= pal[:accent] %>; text-shadow: <%= pal[:mascot_shadow] %>">
    <%= team&.mascot || example.team_slug.titleize %>
  </p>

  <p class="<%= compact ? 'mt-1' : 'mt-2' %>">
    <%# One decimal, NOT format_turf_score. The board's helper drops the decimal on
        a whole number, so Baltimore read "1x" here while the prose two sections
        down called the same value "x1.0" — review flagged the mismatch. The page
        uses ONE notation throughout: suffix, one decimal. %>
    <% if board_style %>
      <span class="font-mono font-bold <%= compact ? 'text-base' : 'text-2xl' %>" style="color: <%= pal[:fg] %>"><%= number_with_precision(example.turf_score, precision: 1) %></span><span class="font-bold <%= compact ? 'text-sm' : 'text-xl' %>" style="color: <%= pal[:fg] %>">x</span>
      <span class="<%= compact ? 'text-[10px]' : 'text-sm' %>" style="color: <%= pal[:fg_faint] %>" data-test="multiplier-label">Points</span>
    <% else %>
      <span class="font-mono font-bold <%= compact ? 'text-base' : 'text-2xl' %>" style="color: <%= pal[:fg] %>"><%= number_with_precision(example.turf_score, precision: 1) %>&times;</span>
      <span class="<%= compact ? 'text-[10px]' : 'text-sm' %>" style="color: <%= pal[:fg_faint] %>">Turf Score</span>
    <% end %>
  </p>

  <div class="<%= compact ? 'mt-2' : 'mt-3' %> flex items-center gap-2" aria-hidden="true">
    <span class="h-px flex-1" style="background-color: <%= pal[:divider] %>"></span>
    <span class="text-xs font-bold" style="color: <%= pal[:fg] %>">vs</span>
    <span class="h-px flex-1" style="background-color: <%= pal[:divider] %>"></span>
  </div>

  <%# grid-template-columns inline, not a Tailwind grid-cols-N class: the column
      count is computed, and Tailwind never sees a computed class name. %>
  <div class="mt-2 grid" style="grid-template-columns: repeat(<%= [example.opponent_slugs.size, 1].max %>, minmax(0, 1fr))">
    <% example.opponent_slugs.each_with_index do |slug, index| %>
      <% opponent = teams[slug] %>
      <div class="px-px lg:px-1 text-center"
           style="<%= "border-left: 1px solid #{pal[:divider]};" if index.positive? %>">
        <p class="text-[9px] uppercase tracking-wide leading-tight" style="color: <%= pal[:grey] %>">Week <%= index + 1 %></p>
        <p class="mt-1 py-1 flex items-center justify-center gap-0.5 leading-none"
           style="background: <%= opponent_label_halo(opponent, team) %>">
          <% if board_style %>
            <span class="text-[10px]"><%= opponent&.emoji %></span>
            <span class="text-[10px] font-semibold whitespace-nowrap" data-test="opponent-abbr"
                  style="color: <%= opponent_label_color(opponent, team) %>"><%= opponent&.short_name || slug.split("-").map { |w| w[0] }.join.upcase.first(3) %></span>
          <% else %>
            <span class="text-[10px] lg:text-sm"><%= opponent&.emoji %></span>
            <span class="text-[10px] lg:text-sm font-semibold truncate"
                  style="color: <%= opponent_label_color(opponent, team) %>"><%= opponent&.short_name || slug.split("-").last.upcase %></span>
          <% end %>
        </p>
      </div>
    <% end %>
  </div>
</div>
<% if board_style %>
</div>
<% end %>
